---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EMAIL, PIKOS } from '../consts';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Staff software engineer at Solace Health. Product, mostly backend, and the standards a team runs on."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm Alex, a staff software engineer at Solace Health, mostly on the
      backend. I've joined three startups early, two of them as the first
      engineer, so I've seen most of the ways a young codebase can go sideways,
      and a few ways to keep it from happening.
    </p>
    <p>
      The problems I like best are the ones a team has learned to live with: the
      dashboard nobody trusts, the bug that keeps coming back. I like finding the
      cause, fixing it with the people who own it, and then making it hard to
      break again with a lint rule, a CI check, or a short written standard.
    </p>
    <p>
      A lot of what I'm proudest of isn't code. At Solace I wrote the process we
      use to plan work across teams, and the backend guide that new hires and
      coding agents both learn from. I've done a lot of the interviewing as the
      team grew, and mentoring is still one of my favorite parts of the job.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside work I'm building <a href={PIKOS.site}>Pikos</a>: notes, tasks and
      calendar in one app, with everything on your device. It's also where I see
      how far coding agents can go. I pick the architecture and make the calls,
      and agents do most of the typing. I also built
      <a href="https://github.com/Alex-AK/hone">Hone</a>, a small practice app
      for keeping my own fundamentals sharp.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you want to talk shop, <a href={EMAIL}>email</a>'s the best way to
      reach me.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.125rem;
  }
</style>
